# name: (when, skeleton, marking, alternatives, errors, examples[ids], er_ids)
T={
'Solve linear equations':("A multi-step setting-up question (areas, perimeters) that ends in a linear equation, or a plain equation with fractions.","1 Write each quantity as an expression. 2 Form one equation. 3 Clear fractions or brackets first. 4 Collect terms in x on one side. 5 Solve and state the value. 6 Substitute back to check.","Process marks for each expression, then for the equation, then an accuracy mark; or a method mark for clearing fractions, a dependent method mark for isolating the unknown, then an accuracy mark.","Any valid algebraic route; an equation written near the working counts only if it is clearly applied.","No Higher-tier report evidence found (UNVERIFIED as advice).",['jun2023-2h-5','nov2019-3h-10'],[]),
'Solve quadratics by factorising or formula':("Equation not yet equal to zero, or asked for exact roots.","1 Rearrange to zero. 2 Factorise, or substitute into the formula. 3 Solve each bracket. 4 State both values.","Method mark for rearranging, method mark for a correct factorisation or formula substitution (one sign slip allowed), accuracy mark for both values.","Formula or factorisation both accepted; rearranging can be implied by correct brackets.","Not rearranging to zero before factorising (report evidence T09).",['nov2021-1h-8'],['T09']),
'Complete the square and turning point':("Write in the form (x-a)^2+b, or find a turning point or maximum.","1 Take out the leading coefficient if it is not 1. 2 Halve the x coefficient, square it. 3 Write the squared bracket and correct the constant. 4 Read the turning point from the bracket and constant.","Process marks for factoring out, starting the square, and finishing it; an accuracy mark; answer alone with no working earns nothing in the scheme read. Follow-through is allowed from the factoring step if only one slip.","Turning point can follow from the student's own values.","Not recognising a complete-the-square question (T10).",['nov2021-1h-22','jun2019-1h-19'],['T10']),
'Simultaneous equations (linear or linear-quadratic)':("Two equations, two unknowns, solve for both.","1 Match coefficients or substitute. 2 Eliminate one variable. 3 Solve it. 4 Substitute back for the other. 5 Check in the other equation.","Method mark to eliminate or substitute (one arithmetic slip allowed), accuracy for one correct value, dependent method mark for finding the second, accuracy for both. Trial and improvement scores nothing unless both values are right.","Elimination or substitution accepted.","Negative signs and order of steps (report, p15 of general report; not a per-question id).",['jun2024-1h-10','nov2022-1h-12'],[]),
'Rearrange formulae':("Make a letter the subject.","1 Clear fractions. 2 Expand brackets. 3 Gather terms in the subject on one side. 4 Factorise if the subject appears twice. 5 Divide.","Method mark for the first correct step, dependent method mark for isolating, a method mark for factorising (needs two terms in the subject), accuracy for the final form.","Any equivalent final form.","None found in report.",['jun2022-3h-2','jun2023-1h-17'],[]),
'Inequalities and regions':("Describe a region, solve an inequality, or explain an error on a number line.","1 Draw each boundary line, solid for or-equal, dashed for strict. 2 Test a point. 3 State each inequality. For a number line, check circle type and the end.","Method marks for each boundary line indicated, accuracy mark for all inequalities together; explanation questions give communication marks for each distinct correct explanation.","Inequality signs accepted in place of equals for the method marks.","Ignoring part of the inequality when drawing it (general report, no id).",['nov2022-2h-16','nov2023-3h-4'],[]),
'Sequences and nth term':("Find or use an nth term, or test whether a number is in a sequence.","1 Find the common difference. 2 Write dn+c, find c. 3 For a test, set the term equal to the number and solve. 4 Conclude yes or no with the term position.","Independent marks for the nth term (a mark for correct form), a method mark for setting up the test, accuracy for the conclusion with working.","Listing terms accepted for the test.","Checking quadratic sequences by substitution (T14).",['nov2022-2h-3'],['T14']),
'Iteration':("Show a rearrangement leads to an iterative formula, then iterate.","1 Rearrange to the given form. 2 Substitute the start value for x1. 3 Substitute again for x2 (and x3). 4 Round as asked.","Communication mark for the rearrangement, method marks for each substitution, accuracy mark in a range.","Working backwards from the given formula is accepted.","No report evidence found.",['jun2023-2h-17','nov2021-2h-16'],[]),
'Algebraic proof':("Prove an identity, or a statement about odd/even or consecutive numbers.","1 Define general numbers (2n+1, 2n and so on). 2 Expand and simplify. 3 Factor out the property. 4 State the conclusion in words.","Method marks for correct expansions, communication marks for the stated conclusion and for a complete proof.","Different algebraic set-ups accepted.","Trying values instead of a general proof (T08).",['nov2022-1h-16','jun2023-2h-18'],['T08']),
'Functions: composite and inverse':("Evaluate fg(x), find the inverse, or combine.","1 For composite: replace the inner function first. 2 For inverse: swap x and y and solve. 3 Check by substitution.","A mark for the first step (add/undo), method marks for substituting or forming the inverse, accuracy.","Inverse operations are accepted; flow charts were less successful (T13).",'Using a flow chart without care (T13).',['jun2022-2h-19','nov2023-2h-19'],['T13']),
'Algebraic fractions':("Simplify or combine fractions with algebraic terms.","1 Factorise every numerator and denominator. 2 Cancel common factors, or find a common denominator. 3 Combine and expand carefully, taking care with the minus sign. 4 Simplify.","Independent mark for factorising, method marks for the common denominator and combined numerator, accuracy.","Incorrect factorising is condoned for later method marks.","Algebra manipulation weakness (report, no id).",['jun2019-2h-13','jun2022-3h-19'],[]),
'Straight-line graphs and equations':("Find the equation of a line, a parallel, or a perpendicular line.","1 Find the gradient. 2 Use y = mx + c or y - y1 = m(x - x1). 3 For a perpendicular, use m1 x m2 = -1. 4 State the equation.","Method marks for the gradient, for starting the equation, accuracy.","Several forms of the line equation accepted.","None found.",['jun2024-1h-6','jun2019-2h-16'],[]),
'Percentage change and reverse percentages':("Increase or decrease by a percentage, or work back to an original value.","1 Write the multiplier. 2 Multiply (or divide for reverse). 3 Answer in the form asked (amount, percentage). 4 Compare the correct bases.","Process marks for the correct first step, a compound process if repeated, accuracy; explanation questions give a communication mark for naming the wrong base.","Percent of original or multiplier methods.","Using the new amount as the base (explanation questions); advice about undoing the multiplier is UNVERIFIED in the report (T18).",['jun2024-3h-4','jun2025-3h-12'],[]),
'Compound interest and growth/decay':("Repeated percentage change over years.","1 Write the multiplier^n. 2 Work year by year if unsure. 3 Subtract if only interest is asked for. 4 Compare totals if two deals.","Process marks for year 1, for compounding, for completion; accuracy mark; communication mark when a decision is asked.","Multiplier or year by year.","Giving total instead of interest (T17).",['jun2023-2h-8','jun2024-3h-14'],['T17']),
'Ratio sharing':("Share an amount, combine ratios, or find an unknown from related ratios.","1 Add the parts. 2 Find the value of one part. 3 Multiply for each share. 4 For linked ratios use a common multiple.","Process marks for combining ratios and forming proportions, a communication mark for the common multiple argument, accuracy.","Two-way tables, probability trees or cube counts accepted.","Picking the quantity asked for (T20).",['jun2019-1h-6','jun2019-2h-17'],['T20']),
'Direct and inverse proportion':("Formulas with k, or inverse square relationships.","1 Write y = kx, y = k/x^2 or y = k square root. 2 Substitute known values to find k. 3 Use k to answer. 4 Keep separate k for separate relations.","Process mark for the relation, for substitution, for the full process; accuracy.","Condones proportional symbol for the first two marks.","Direct versus inverse mix-ups and reusing one constant (T19).",['jun2019-1h-20','jun2024-2h-12'],['T19']),
'Speed, density and pressure':("Compound measures and unit changes.","1 Check units. 2 Use the formula triangle. 3 Compute each part. 4 Combine, then divide for an average.","Process marks for each part, for combining, for the final process; accuracy; consistent units are required.","Working in ml or cm3 is accepted if consistent.","Using division where multiplication is needed (T21).",['jun2019-3h-13','jun2022-3h-6'],['T21']),
'Bounds and error intervals':("A value rounded to a given accuracy used in a calculation.","1 Write lower and upper bounds of each input. 2 Choose the bound that gives the maximum or minimum. 3 Compute. 4 Give the answer to a justified accuracy.","Independent mark for a bound, method marks for using the right bounds, accuracy, and a communication mark for the rounded conclusion.","Truncated bounds accepted to at least 4 significant figures.","Wrong bound or average-of-bounds (T05).",['nov2019-2h-20','nov2020-3h-18'],['T05']),
'Standard form':("Convert, or add, subtract, multiply.","1 Write in a x 10^n form with 1 <= a < 10. 2 Common power for add/subtract. 3 Calculate. 4 Standard form answer.","Independent marks for conversions, method mark for the calculation, accuracy; a correct answer in the wrong form earns the method mark only.","Both numbers over a common power accepted.","None noted (done well).",['jun2022-1h-4','jun2024-3h-2'],[]),
'Surds and rationalising':("Exact answers with roots.","1 Simplify each surd. 2 Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate or root. 3 Expand carefully. 4 Collect and give the required form.","Method marks for rationalising, for expanding, accuracy mark; a process mark may be earned wherever it appears.","Writing as a single fraction first accepted.","Rationalising not completed, wrong simplification (T07).",['jun2023-1h-23','nov2020-1h-20'],['T07']),
'Recurring decimals to fractions':("Convert a recurring decimal.","1 Let x equal the decimal. 2 Multiply by 10, 100 or 1000. 3 Subtract to remove the repeat. 4 Solve and simplify.","Method mark for a correct multiple, dependent method mark for subtracting to a terminating decimal, communication mark in proofs; terminating decimals of five digits score no proof credit.","Any correct pair of multiples.","None found.",['jun2022-1h-12','jun2023-3h-20'],[]),
'Indices':("Powers, reciprocals, roots, fractional powers.","1 Convert roots to fractional powers. 2 Apply index laws one at a time. 3 Evaluate or leave in index form. 4 Give a reason if asked.","Method marks for each correct law application, accuracy, communication mark for reasoning.","Any correct order of laws.","Handled well generally (report).",['jun2022-1h-18','jun2022-3h-9'],[]),
'Pythagoras':("Find a missing side or perimeter, or use it in a proof.","1 Identify the hypotenuse. 2 Square, add or subtract. 3 Square root. 4 Add lengths for the perimeter.","Process marks to start, to complete the hypotenuse, to finish the perimeter; accuracy mark.","None needed.","Assuming right angles when none exist (T25).",['nov2021-2h-5','jun2022-1h-13'],['T25']),
'Right-angled trigonometry':("Missing sides or angles; multi-step.","1 Label opposite, adjacent, hypotenuse. 2 Pick sin, cos or tan. 3 Substitute and rearrange. 4 Use inverse for angles. 5 Give to the accuracy asked.","Process marks for each trigonometric step and for combining; accuracy mark in a range; other methods allowed if they reach a single unknown.","Alternative methods accepted if they lead to one equation in one unknown.","Exact values known (T29).",['nov2019-2h-12','nov2021-2h-6'],['T29']),
'Sine rule, cosine rule and area formula':("Non-right-angled triangles.","1 Mark known sides and angles. 2 Choose sine rule, cosine rule or area. 3 Substitute and compute. 4 Chain results if two steps.","Method marks for the cosine rule, correct order of operations, the sine rule (dependent), accuracy.","Sine or cosine rule order can vary.","Identifying the wrong angle.",['jun2022-2h-18','jun2023-2h-13'],[]),
'3D trigonometry and bearings':("Angles in solids or bearings problems.","1 Draw the right-angled triangle inside the solid. 2 Find any needed length by Pythagoras. 3 Use a trigonometric ratio. 4 State the angle asked.","Process marks for lengths, for the trigonometric statement, accuracy.","Several valid triangle routes.","Not knowing which angle to find (T24); bearing from the wrong point (T26).",['jun2019-2h-19','nov2022-2h-20'],['T24','T26']),
'Circle theorems':("Angle chains with reasons.","1 Mark known angles. 2 Name the theorem for each step. 3 Write the reason in words using the key terms. 4 State the final angle.","Method marks for angle steps, accuracy, then a communication mark for a relevant theorem named; key words (centre, circumference, tangent) are required.","Different chains of angles accepted.","Wrong theorem, reasons badly worded (T23).",['jun2022-2h-20','jun2023-1h-21'],['T23']),
'Vectors and vector proofs':("Express vectors or prove parallel/collinear.","1 Write a route. 2 Use the ratio along a line. 3 Simplify. 4 For proof, show one vector is a multiple of another and state the conclusion.","Process marks for each route, accuracy; proof marks for method, a bold statement and the complete conclusion.","Any valid route accepted.","Part (b) was hard (report, 2h q20).",['jun2023-2h-20','nov2020-1h-21'],[]),
'Transformations':("Describe or perform transformations.","1 Name the single transformation. 2 Give all aspects (angle, direction, centre; scale factor, centre; mirror line; vector). 3 Draw to a clear position.","Independent marks per transformation or per two aspects; more than one transformation described scores zero.","Equivalent descriptions accepted (270 clockwise).","Translations weak (report).",['jun2025-1h-9','nov2020-3h-11'],[]),
'Similarity, congruence and scale factors':("Compare lengths, areas, volumes.","1 Find the length scale factor. 2 Square for area, cube for volume. 3 Apply. 4 State the ratio in simplest form.","Method mark for the factor, process marks for squaring or cubing, accuracy.","Decimals or fractions accepted.","Linking scale factors in unfamiliar settings (T22).",['jun2019-2h-9','jun2024-2h-17'],['T22']),
'Loci and constructions':("Constructions with compasses.","1 Use compasses, keep arcs. 2 Draw the line. 3 Do not erase construction lines.","Two communication marks; one for a line within tolerance, one for a fully correct construction with arcs.","None.","None found.",['nov2019-1h-4','nov2023-1h-5'],[]),
'Probability trees':("Combined events, with or without replacement.","1 Put probabilities on each branch. 2 Multiply along branches. 3 Add the relevant outcomes. 4 Check by 1 minus.","Independent marks for branch values, method mark for a correct path product, accuracy.","1 minus the complement is credited.","At least read as both outcomes (T30).",['jun2022-3h-21','jun2024-3h-6'],['T30']),
'Venn diagrams and conditional probability':("Sets and probabilities from a Venn diagram.","1 Fill the overlap first. 2 Then each set only. 3 Total check. 4 Probability = count over relevant total.","Independent marks for regions, method mark for the probability, accuracy.","Follow-through from the student's diagram.","Set notation in part b (T35).",['jun2019-3h-1','jun2023-1h-5'],['T35']),
'Averages from tables':("Mean, median or mode from data.","1 Use midpoints for grouped data. 2 Multiply by frequency. 3 Total, divide by total frequency. 4 Comment in context.","Method mark for products, method mark for total over frequency, accuracy; a communication mark for comparison or effect on the mean.","Process marks accepted for total-sum methods.","Frequency table confusion (report, general).",['nov2023-1h-4','nov2023-3h-3'],[]),
'Histograms':("Frequency density.","1 Frequency density = frequency / width. 2 Use area for frequency. 3 Total, then proportion.","Method marks for area represents frequency and for totals, accuracy.","Any consistent area unit.","Using bar height for frequency (T33, partly supported).",['jun2019-3h-21','jun2023-2h-16'],['T33']),
'Cumulative frequency and box plots':("Quartiles, medians and comparisons.","1 Read median, LQ, UQ at the right cumulative values. 2 Compute IQR. 3 Compare in context with a sentence.","Independent marks for readings, communication marks for comparison; follow-through from readings.","Acceptable comparison wordings are given in the scheme.","Done well in the report (2h q11).",['jun2019-1h-11','nov2021-2h-9'],[]),
'Scatter graphs':("Correlation, line of best fit, estimate.","1 Describe correlation in words. 2 Draw a line of best fit. 3 Read from the line. 4 Comment on reliability or outliers.","Independent mark for plotting, a communication mark for correlation, a method mark for the line, accuracy within a range.","Tolerance on reading.","None found.",['nov2021-3h-1','nov2022-2h-1'],[]),
}
